# Copy to .env before first start:  cp .env.example .env && $EDITOR .env
#
# Grafana's admin password. Compose requires this for EVERY subcommand
# (up, down, config) — an unset value fails loudly rather than silently
# falling back to admin/admin.
#
# IMPORTANT: Grafana only applies this when it initialises its database for
# the first time. If the grafana-data volume already exists, the password it
# was created with stays in force and this value is ignored — so changing it
# later does nothing until you `docker compose down -v` (which deletes the
# volume and its dashboards' local edits). Verified 2026-08-11: with a
# pre-existing volume, admin/admin still authenticated while the new password
# was rejected.
# Deliberately empty. Compose's ${VAR:?} treats empty and unset alike, so
# copying this file without editing it fails loudly at start-up rather than
# quietly bringing up Grafana with a password someone forgot to change.
GF_SECURITY_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
